Dear Yuchao,

Yet again another question for you regarding CODEX!

I'm trying to call CNVs on a Trios done using the Nextera AllExome Kit.

The trios consists of 2 female and one male, and I'm getting this error on chrY:
> qcObj <- qc(Y, sampname, chr, ref, mapp, gc, cov_thresh = c(20, 4000), length_thresh = c(20, 2000), mapp_thresh = 0.9, gc_thresh = c(20, 80))
>
> Error in apply(Y_qc, 1, median) : dim(X) must have a positive length

Considering that I only have one male sample, I figure that it won't be possible to call a CNV on chrY, since coverage normalization will probably be biased from the absence of reads on female subjects. Anyway, is there a way to get rid of the error?

Moreover, when calling CNVs on allosomes, should I choose a number of maximum latent Poisson factors equal to the number of male or females that I have in my sample pool? E.g.: with 3 males and 4 females, should K = 1:3 in normObj?

Do you have some best practices for allosomes in general?

Again, thanks for your thoughtful help and your time,

All Best,

Daniele

