Hi Daniele,

CODEX is a multi-sample normalization method that estimates Poisson latent factors across samples and exons. You only have 3 samples and CODEX won’t be the method of choice for you. For CODEX to perform well, we recommend having at least 10-20 samples. Also for sex chromosomes, CODEX is currently not able to handle it well, especially for Y chromosome. The error you see might be due to the fact no exons pass the QC procedure and thus the dimension of the Y_qc is 0 and leads to an error. Again, 3 samples as input for CODEX is not ideal.

Let me know if you have further questions,
Yuchao

